WEBVTT

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:14.960
I wonder what's wrong.

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:16.210
Since he had had that talk with NK,
things seem kind of tense.

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:19.580
"CELL"
"WHITE BLOOD CELL"
Since he had had that talk with NK,
things seem kind of tense.

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:24.420
--Not looking good.
--It's gone to ruin, all right.

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:26.420
I-I can't breathe!

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:30.750
This is toxic gas from the harmful bacteria
that live in the intestines.

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:33.540
--"Toxic gas"?
--"Toxic gas"?

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:35.750
So, his friends are all here?

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:41.880
Yeah. There are up to a hundred trillion
bacteria in the intestines, they say.

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:44.170
Then, we're sure to find them, right?

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:45.420
Yeah.

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:47.170
That'll be a relief.

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:50.710
He doesn't sound the least bit relieved.

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:54.620
Look, you two, I don't care what
you do as long as you're quiet.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:57.420
I don't want him to know we're on the move.

00:00:57.420 --> 00:00:59.830
Now, I've fought with him once in the past.

00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:05.000
And I'm going to use that experience today
to head to the front lines as a Memory T Cell

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:06.420
and finish off the enemy!

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:09.540
U-Um, I just have a simple question.

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:13.250
Who's this guy you keep mentioning?

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:16.290
--A Cancer Cell.
--A Cancer Cell.

00:01:16.290 --> 00:01:19.080
C-Cancer Cell?

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.500
Are you okay, Platelet?

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:25.210
Yes! I'm fine!

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:27.210
Everyone! Watch out, okay?

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:29.250
I can't see in front of me!

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:33.080
"PLATELETS"

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:37.750
It looks like he's meeting us head-on this time.

00:01:51.330 --> 00:01:52.960
Where is he?

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:03.830
You really came back to life just so you could
throw a tantrum, you stupid Cancer Cell?

00:02:03.830 --> 00:02:05.830
Die!

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:11.040
Did I get him?

00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:17.500
So, you fell for it! He's nothing but a puppet!

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:20.580
Look at all the effort you had
to put in against a mere doll.

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:24.750
Do you know what you've gotten
yourselves into, Immune Cells?

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:35.330
I'm so thrilled!

00:02:35.330 --> 00:02:38.170
It's the trio from before, right?

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:40.920
Cancer Cell!

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:43.170
It's been a long time, huh?

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:46.420
This just might be what they call fate, huh?

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:50.210
For the three of you from that day
to saunter right toward me.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:56.880
Now then, which of us, me or you three,
is on the side of justice?

00:02:57.790 --> 00:03:00.500
Let's settle it once and for all.

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:01.670
Here he comes!

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:05.460
Die! Die!

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:07.710
NK!

00:04:55.000 --> 00:05:00.000
"EPISODE 7:
CANCER CELL II (PART I)"

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:17.170
You really are a one-trick pony
when it comes to attacking!

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:18.830
You saved us, NK!

00:05:18.830 --> 00:05:23.000
Hey! You can gloat after you've untied us!

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:27.580
Now then... Boy, would you mind
telling me something?

00:05:27.580 --> 00:05:32.330
Why'd you come back to life
when you knew you'd only be killed?

00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:35.880
Don't tell me you actually thought
you could win this time!

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:38.670
This is my second time battling you!

00:05:38.670 --> 00:05:44.790
Your tactics are a little too exposed for you
to be picking a fight with me, you know.

00:05:44.790 --> 00:05:48.000
It's not that I want to pick a fight with you.

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:52.170
It's just that I've found
what it is I have to do.

00:05:52.170 --> 00:05:56.920
And I wanted you three to bear witness.

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:25.620
Surprised? These are all the same
as that puppet you just saw.

00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:28.620
They're all fragments of my tissue.

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:31.120
You can stab them with your sword,
but they won't die.

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:33.500
They'll keep moving forever.

00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:39.670
There isn't a thing that you can do.
Just resign yourselves to being my captives.

00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:01.460
Behind you, NK!

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:06.500
Over by you, too, Neutrophil!

00:07:12.830 --> 00:07:14.880
Who do you think you're dealing with?

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:19.170
I'm Memory T Cell, and I've seen
every one of your attacks!

00:07:19.170 --> 00:07:21.880
Memory T Cell...

00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:23.460
I see.

00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:26.710
Meaning you're not quite
the same guy you were before?

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:27.960
You can't escape!

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:33.540
Right now, I can foresee your every next move!

00:07:33.540 --> 00:07:35.500
Right there!

00:07:38.500 --> 00:07:41.380
Kindly cease your attacks.

00:07:41.380 --> 00:07:44.420
Those are not the appropriate responses.

00:07:44.420 --> 00:07:47.620
He is not an enemy from the outside world.

00:07:47.620 --> 00:07:49.790
He was born of this body.

00:07:49.790 --> 00:07:52.620
He's a cell just like us.

00:07:52.620 --> 00:07:56.580
I will not allow any attacks on the body itself.

00:07:56.580 --> 00:08:00.000
R-Regulatory T Cell...

00:08:01.170 --> 00:08:03.580
Regulatory T Cells.

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:09.580
They control the activity of T Cells to prevent
them from triggering anomalous immune responses.

00:08:09.580 --> 00:08:11.830
Wh-Why...

00:08:11.830 --> 00:08:13.710
...would you...

00:08:25.170 --> 00:08:26.920
No good! Memory T!

00:08:26.920 --> 00:08:28.380
Watch your back!

00:08:34.210 --> 00:08:36.710
N-Neutrophil!

00:08:45.380 --> 00:08:48.620
...146, where are you? Come in!

00:08:48.620 --> 00:08:50.670
1146! Where are you?

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:51.580
Just as I thought.

00:08:51.580 --> 00:08:54.960
Come in, 1146! Come in--

00:08:54.960 --> 00:08:58.670
I knew you'd protect him.
I was sure you would.

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:08.750
Let's have a nice, long chat...
instead of killing each other.

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:10.080
Okay?

00:09:17.080 --> 00:09:19.290
Nyuuu! Nyuuu!

00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:22.000
Are those germs still behind us?

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:23.250
I'm not sure!

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:25.330
Just keep running!

00:09:29.170 --> 00:09:33.120
Nyuuu!

00:09:41.880 --> 00:09:46.290
We're going to keep our handkerchiefs pressed
to our mouths and run low to the ground!

00:09:46.290 --> 00:09:47.670
Okay!

00:09:50.420 --> 00:09:54.460
It looks like the intestine is in
even worse shape than before.

00:10:00.380 --> 00:10:02.250
Big Sister Red Blood Cell...

00:10:02.250 --> 00:10:03.170
What is it?

00:10:03.170 --> 00:10:07.210
You see, you see... I don't think
we can take this path.

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:08.330
See? Look!

00:10:08.330 --> 00:10:08.710
"NO ENTRY"
See? Look!

00:10:08.710 --> 00:10:10.250
"NO ENTRY"
You can't come this way!

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:12.420
The bacteria's invaded the area up ahead!

00:10:12.420 --> 00:10:13.330
What?

00:10:13.330 --> 00:10:15.830
Take another route and run as fast as you can!

00:10:15.830 --> 00:10:17.540
R-Right!

00:10:17.540 --> 00:10:18.750
I'm so scared...

00:10:18.750 --> 00:10:21.460
Big Sister Red Blood Cell!

00:10:21.460 --> 00:10:25.080
We're going to be fine, Backward Cap.

00:10:25.080 --> 00:10:28.620
The Platelets seem really anxious.

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:30.880
I have to be their rock now!

00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:33.290
You guys, we're going to run
at top speed, okay?

00:10:33.290 --> 00:10:35.000
Okay!

00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:52.790
NK! Memory T!

00:10:55.170 --> 00:10:57.500
Cancer Cell!

00:11:13.040 --> 00:11:15.040
Memory T!

00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:17.330
Let me out of here, Cancer Cell!

00:11:17.330 --> 00:11:19.670
Wasn't I the one you wanted to kill?

00:11:19.670 --> 00:11:23.210
If you have a grudge against me,
then I'll take you on!

00:11:23.210 --> 00:11:25.790
That won't do, White Blood Cell.

00:11:25.790 --> 00:11:28.210
You shouldn't fly off the handle
when you're all banged up.

00:11:28.210 --> 00:11:31.210
You need to value your own life more.

00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:37.750
If you agree to what I'm about to say,
I'll let you out of there right away.

00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:44.750
Since I'm sure it's tearing you apart
to be locked up and helpless.

00:11:44.750 --> 00:11:48.000
Regulatory T Cell, open this door, will you?

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:52.500
I'll do it! I'll kill this
Cancer Cell! So please!

00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:56.790
Kill? I can't open that door
if you're going to kill him.

00:11:56.790 --> 00:12:00.000
As he's in no way an external enemy.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:02.710
Regulatory T Cell's role.

00:12:02.710 --> 00:12:06.670
Regulatory T Cells are responsible
for reining in the activity of Immune Cells,

00:12:06.670 --> 00:12:09.040
preventing them from attacking the body's

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:12.710
own tissues or cells that
are beneficial to the body.

00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:16.710
In this case, as the Cancer Cell
originated from this body,

00:12:16.710 --> 00:12:19.670
instead of recognizing him as
a foreign substance, a non-self cell,

00:12:19.670 --> 00:12:23.540
she is trying to suppress
the Immune Cells' attacks.

00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:28.750
It's not like she's betraying you guys.

00:12:28.750 --> 00:12:32.830
This is that lady's job, I hear.

00:12:32.830 --> 00:12:37.120
Cancer Cell, I'm gonna kill--

00:12:37.120 --> 00:12:38.580
You mustn't...

00:12:38.580 --> 00:12:41.920
...ever attack other cells.

00:12:41.920 --> 00:12:43.460
Isn't this amusing?

00:12:43.460 --> 00:12:47.830
You normal cells are all so dead serious.

00:12:47.830 --> 00:12:51.380
And yet, despite being dead serious...

00:12:51.380 --> 00:12:53.040
White Blood Cell...

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:57.830
...you rescued that ordinary cell
and those Lactic Acid Bacteria, didn't you?

00:12:57.830 --> 00:13:00.540
About that... The only reason I didn't kill them

00:13:00.540 --> 00:13:03.250
was because those bacteria
weren't toxic to this body! That's all!

00:13:03.250 --> 00:13:06.500
Sure. I get that, all right.

00:13:06.500 --> 00:13:12.500
But the thing is, I've changed my mind
somewhat. It got me thinking.

00:13:12.500 --> 00:13:15.920
Lives that are necessary
and lives that are not...

00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:19.620
Why does such a distinction
have to made at all?

00:13:19.620 --> 00:13:24.380
When it's so tragic for us to be taking lives
or being robbed of our lives,

00:13:24.380 --> 00:13:29.750
why do we have to keep repeating
that cycle over and over again?

00:13:29.750 --> 00:13:33.670
What do you think?
Have you ever had a thought like that?

00:13:33.670 --> 00:13:35.420
It's for the sake of this body!

00:13:35.420 --> 00:13:39.880
Because it's necessary!
That's why we die and kill!

00:13:39.880 --> 00:13:42.170
That's what I thought you'd say.

00:13:42.170 --> 00:13:45.170
Okay, then let's take it a bit further.

00:13:45.170 --> 00:13:48.080
Which is more important?

00:13:48.080 --> 00:13:51.000
The lives of trillions of cells?

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:54.330
Or this body's one life?

00:13:55.920 --> 00:14:00.170
We cells are killed, burn with hatred
for each other and are sacrificed

00:14:00.170 --> 00:14:03.500
all so that this body can go on living.

00:14:03.500 --> 00:14:08.750
Those of us who get killed, and you guys,
the ones who kill... We've all suffered so much.

00:14:08.750 --> 00:14:14.420
So, how about a world where we cells
don't have to kill or be killed at all?

00:14:14.420 --> 00:14:19.750
Even if it's a world gone mad,
approaching death...

00:14:19.750 --> 00:14:23.120
If it's to make that world a reality
even for a split second...

00:14:23.120 --> 00:14:27.500
...don't you think we'd be justified
in sacrificing the life of this body?

00:14:27.500 --> 00:14:31.290
I won't let you! No way will
I ever let you do such a thing!

00:14:31.290 --> 00:14:33.210
Let me out of here, Cancer Cell!

00:14:33.210 --> 00:14:37.330
I'll kill you! You're horrendously wrong,
but I'll set you straight!

00:14:37.330 --> 00:14:42.670
If this body dies, that means that
all of us cells will die with it, too!

00:14:42.670 --> 00:14:44.080
Sure, we'll die.

00:14:44.080 --> 00:14:46.420
But we'll die after we've been liberated.

00:14:46.420 --> 00:14:50.000
And it's my job to make that happen.

00:14:50.000 --> 00:14:51.960
There's nothing wrong about that at all.

00:14:51.960 --> 00:14:54.170
There's no way you could pull that off--

00:14:54.170 --> 00:14:56.000
Oh, I can pull it off.

00:14:57.750 --> 00:15:03.040
Regulatory T Cell is siding with me.
Not to mention...

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:05.250
...this place, as well.

00:15:20.120 --> 00:15:23.040
Th-Those fumes are...

00:15:24.420 --> 00:15:26.250
...harmful bacteria...

00:15:26.250 --> 00:15:27.710
...toxins!

00:15:33.500 --> 00:15:36.420
When the new world is completed...

00:15:36.420 --> 00:15:42.540
...then let's be friends, all right,
White Blood Cell, you kindhearted assassin?

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:44.040
Stop!

00:16:08.620 --> 00:16:11.290
Don't do it, Cancer Cell!

00:16:27.040 --> 00:16:31.290
NK! Memory T! Regulatory T Cell!
Are you all right?

00:16:31.290 --> 00:16:33.170
Y-Yeah!

00:16:34.580 --> 00:16:38.670
So, you're more worried
about your friends than yourself?

00:16:38.670 --> 00:16:45.380
You know, that's what I like about you
along with all the contradictions you bear.

00:16:45.380 --> 00:16:48.080
Even though you can only live
for someone else's sake,

00:16:48.080 --> 00:16:52.380
you were born a cell who can
do nothing but kill others.

00:16:52.380 --> 00:16:57.500
Watching you, I feel such pity and impatience.

00:16:57.500 --> 00:16:58.460
And it's so entertaining.

00:16:58.460 --> 00:17:00.420
How dare you!

00:17:01.960 --> 00:17:07.000
I'm sick of all your yammering,
you annoying little punk!

00:17:13.210 --> 00:17:16.380
Cancer Cell, I'm gonna kill--

00:17:16.380 --> 00:17:18.000
You mustn't...

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:19.880
...ever attack other cells.

00:17:19.880 --> 00:17:23.380
Do you realize you've been repeating
the same conversation over and over?

00:17:23.380 --> 00:17:25.670
--What are you, a moron?
--Sh-Shut the cell up!

00:17:25.670 --> 00:17:27.500
As if... I had time...

00:17:27.500 --> 00:17:30.670
...to think... of different lines...
every single time!

00:17:30.670 --> 00:17:31.830
I totally agree.

00:17:31.830 --> 00:17:33.460
In the first place...

00:17:33.460 --> 00:17:36.620
...is that the only move you've got,
pounding him head-on?

00:17:36.620 --> 00:17:40.210
Can you at least try a different
move for once, you idiot?

00:17:40.210 --> 00:17:45.120
Shut up! This is how I've always been, moron!

00:17:45.120 --> 00:17:46.750
That's right.

00:17:46.750 --> 00:17:49.750
This is how you've always been.

00:17:49.750 --> 00:17:52.000
Tactics were never your strong suit.

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:56.290
Easily swayed by your emotions,
unable to thrive on victory,

00:17:56.290 --> 00:17:59.040
and unable to use defeat as a stepping-stone...

00:18:02.210 --> 00:18:04.790
You will never be able to defeat me like that.

00:18:04.790 --> 00:18:06.830
It's futile to even struggle.

00:18:06.830 --> 00:18:09.670
Just let it go and cease your attacks.

00:18:11.420 --> 00:18:12.790
Nyuuu!

00:18:28.460 --> 00:18:31.330
W-We're surrounded! What should I do?

00:18:31.330 --> 00:18:33.460
"TREMBLE TREMBLE"
Nyuuu!

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:35.620
Lactic acid bacteria.

00:18:35.620 --> 00:18:38.880
Good bacteria that work to support
the health of the human body.

00:18:38.880 --> 00:18:41.620
They have a variety of features.

00:18:42.540 --> 00:18:44.540
It's all right, Lactic Acid Bacterium!

00:18:44.540 --> 00:18:46.750
I'll p-protect--

00:18:46.750 --> 00:18:50.880
Huh! This cell just said he's going
to protect that lactic acid bacterium!

00:18:50.880 --> 00:18:53.170
That's pretty funny, you know.

00:18:53.170 --> 00:18:54.620
Harmful bacteria.

00:18:54.620 --> 00:18:59.120
Pathogenic E. coli, Staphylococci,
Clostridium and the like

00:18:59.120 --> 00:19:03.250
cause proteins to degrade
and produce toxic by-products.

00:19:03.250 --> 00:19:06.790
Why don't we test you to see
if you can really protect it?

00:19:06.790 --> 00:19:08.830
I wonder if you can withstand this.

00:19:08.830 --> 00:19:11.830
The Harmful Bacteria Toxic Attack!

00:19:11.830 --> 00:19:13.790
Nyuuu!

00:19:13.790 --> 00:19:16.210
The toxicity of harmful bacteria.

00:19:16.210 --> 00:19:18.670
Toxic effects of harmful bacteria

00:19:18.670 --> 00:19:25.540
include intestinal putrefaction,
production of toxins and carcinogens.

00:19:25.540 --> 00:19:32.170
A host of deleterious effects to the human body
can ensue, such as a weakened immune system,

00:19:32.170 --> 00:19:36.580
foul-smelling stools and gas,
and diarrhea or constipation.

00:19:38.540 --> 00:19:41.830
--My legs!
--Nyuuu!

00:19:41.830 --> 00:19:44.830
Show us a good time, Cell boy!

00:19:44.830 --> 00:19:47.000
We came all this way to this side
of the intestinal wall

00:19:47.000 --> 00:19:52.210
only to find it duller than we thought,
so it's been a real gut punch for us!

00:19:53.290 --> 00:19:58.250
We're going to torment you every which way,
so be sure to show us some juicy reactions!

00:19:58.250 --> 00:20:00.460
Nyuuu! Nyu-nyuuu!

00:20:02.620 --> 00:20:04.290
Nyuuu!

00:20:05.500 --> 00:20:07.750
Nyuuu!

00:20:08.710 --> 00:20:10.750
What kind of a lame attack is this?

00:20:10.750 --> 00:20:13.290
Nyuuu!

00:20:13.290 --> 00:20:14.960
Lactic Acid Bacterium!

00:20:19.790 --> 00:20:20.960
Nyuuu!

00:20:20.960 --> 00:20:23.540
Huh! You miserable good bacteria runt...

00:20:23.540 --> 00:20:26.880
You're a germ,
and yet you're sucking up to a cell?

00:20:26.880 --> 00:20:29.620
If you dare turn on us,
I'll obliterate you first!

00:20:29.620 --> 00:20:31.170
Nyuuu! Nyuuu!

00:20:31.170 --> 00:20:34.920
Stay away, Lactic Acid Bacterium!
Just run away as far as you can!

00:20:34.920 --> 00:20:35.920
Nyuuu?

00:20:35.920 --> 00:20:39.790
Don't worry about me!
Just run and save yourself! Hurry!

00:20:39.790 --> 00:20:43.250
Nyuuu! Nyuuu! Nyuuu!

00:20:43.250 --> 00:20:44.710
You dummy! Go now!

00:20:44.710 --> 00:20:46.460
Hey, he's...

00:20:46.460 --> 00:20:49.580
Get out of here now! I said go!

00:20:53.460 --> 00:20:56.250
Nyuuu...

00:20:56.250 --> 00:21:00.380
Get out of my sight!

00:21:02.380 --> 00:21:08.540
Nyuuu!

00:21:08.540 --> 00:21:12.380
Huh! Now that was one lame farce
you made us watch.

00:21:12.380 --> 00:21:17.580
Sorry that you were the only one
who got such a sad goodbye.

